<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central Intelligence Agency</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CIA</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) is the foreign intelligence service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, created by the National Security Act of 1947. Besides gathering intelligence it carried out covert operations during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>, including the 1953 coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> that overthrew Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-mosaddegh">Mohammad Mosaddegh</a>, the 1954 coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a> and the failed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-pigs-invasion">Bay of Pigs invasion</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-intelligence-agency.jpg" alt="Central Intelligence Agency" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Federal government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_Central_Intelligence_Agency.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
